issues.description:
cli/internal/tui/move.go:465-486 builds the D1=B three-option Select with long labels ('Launch --fast · will run: claude "<cmd>"  (token-lean gogo-fast pipeline)'), and cli/internal/tui/modal.go:27 caps the form width at modalMaxFormW=120. Measured against the real Model.View() (go test -overlay probes, no product file touched): the label needs a form width of 86 + len(slug) columns (34 chars of prefix + 9 for '/gogo:go ' + 7 for ' --fast' + 1 quote + 33 for the trailing note + the 2-column cursor gutter), and the form width is min(120, termW-12). So the option list renders complete only when termW >= 98 + len(slug), and NEVER when len(slug) > 34. Concretely, all confirmed by driving m.View():
  - slug 'next' (the only fixture slug) at 200x40 and 120x30: all three options visible - which is why the new suite is green;
  - slug 'next' at 100x24 and 80x24: 'Cancel' is absent and the '--fast' label is cut mid-line;
  - this feature's own 36-char slug at 200x40 (the biggest size tested): 'Cancel' is absent;
  - the M-force confirm (a FORCING description) at 60x12 and 70x14 - sizes at/above the modal's own named minimum, where the modal IS attempted: NO launch option renders at all, just title + description + huh's help line.
Mechanism (verified in the vendored deps): huh sizes the group from group.rawHeight() - one line per option, computed pre-wrap - then Group.WithHeight clamps the field (huh@v1.0.0/group.go:127-139) and Select.updateViewportHeight sets viewport.Height = height - title - description (huh@v1.0.0/field_select.go:526-544). The viewport is therefore ~3 ROWS for 3 options, so any wrapped label pushes the tail out of view. The old 0.35.0 Confirm could not show this defect (Launch/Cancel are one row) and the unsized fallback path cannot either (height<=0 sizes the viewport to the RENDERED height, which is why 'Cancel' is present in the 46x9 fallback) - so this is a regression introduced by D1=B + the modal's WindowSizeMsg layout. Note the labels also carry the source's gate-skip params, so a source with --skip-acceptance --skip-uat loses another 30 characters of slug budget. Cancel is still REACHABLE (down-arrow scrolls the viewport, esc aborts), so this is not a dead end - but the option the user was told to pick from is invisible with no scroll cue. It defeats the exact reason D1=B was chosen over D1=A ('maximally discoverable, both launch modes are visible'), it breaks the plan's own acceptance signal (the box shows the command it will run) and code-review-standards.md #8 (a user-visible state a handler sets must actually be RENDERED by View()). The new tests cannot see it: the only fixture slug is 4 chars, TestModalNeverExceedsTheTerminal measures widths/heights only, and TestOverlayKeepsEveryFormLine compares the composite against m.form.View() - which has ALREADY dropped the option (standards #11: a test that passes for a weaker reason than it claims).

ROUND-2 VERIFICATION (independently re-measured, go test -overlay, no product file touched). Every round-1 cell is now clean, and the fix was probed beyond the cells originally reported (slug 'next' AND this feature's 36-char slug, crossed with the fixture root /r/web AND this repo's real 37-char root, forced and unforced, at 200x40 / 120x30 / 100x24 / 80x24 / 70x14 / 60x12): all three options render in Model.View() in every one of those 48 cells except a narrow band at the modal's own minimum, which is filed separately as REV-006. The title carries the exact command in all 48 (`will run: claude "..."`), the TitleFunc closure captures the heap-stable *formBinding (probe: the pointer is identical after a value-copy of the Model, and the flip is visible through the original copy - TEST-001 holds), and the title updates LIVE in both directions as the cursor moves (Launch -> Launch --fast -> Cancel -> back, each step re-rendered through launch.SetFastParam, so FR4's one-producer property survives). forcingNote() keeps the cap and the blocking slugs verbatim ('FORCING past the source cap - cap 1 reached in web - already building busy') and drops only the remedy tail + rule clause. Both new tests were MUTATION-CHECKED against a scratch copy of the tree: restoring the round-1 command-carrying labels fails TestGoSelectShowsAllThreeOptions at all four sizes, and making forcingNote a pass-through fails TestForcedGoSelectShowsALaunchOptionAtTheModalMinimum. Status -> verified.
